Imagine you are driving a car with 4 seats.
You are given trips in this format:
[passengers, pickup location, drop location]
For example:
[2, 1, 5]
This means:
- Pick up 2 passengers at kilometer 1.
- Drop them off at kilometer 5.
Your job is to check whether the car ever carries more passengers than its capacity.
If it does, return false. Otherwise, return true.

so basically we are ,storing the changes at each loaction, like add at this location and subtract at this 
, and then in the next loop , we add each chnages with passengers , and if passengers exceeds capacity, we return false


class Solution {
    public boolean carPooling(int[][] trips, int capacity) {

        int[] changes = new int[1001];

        // Record pickups and drop-offs
        for (int[] trip : trips) {
            int passengers = trip[0];
            int from = trip[1];
            int to = trip[2];

            changes[from] += passengers;
            changes[to] -= passengers;
        }

        // Calculate the running passenger count
        int passengers = 0;

        for (int i = 0; i <= 1000; i++) {
            passengers += changes[i];

            if (passengers > capacity) {
                return false;
            }
        }

        return true;
    }
}
